          "heading": "Preserve the later obligations",
          "body": "Ordinary journal retention continues for ten years after the last chronicled act, subject to authorized transfer provisions. Resignation also requires notice of the journal's location and triggers the stamp-disabling duty. MCA 1-5-632 independently prohibits intentional withholding of the notary's stamp, journal or commission certificate. A practical departure plan should identify the last chronicled act and any authorized repository arrangement. The retention period follows that record even when the former employer stops operating or changes its records vendor."
